<p class="words">A company reports its <b>earnings</b> four times a year, and the stock often jumps or drops the next morning. Before the report, option prices show how big a move traders are paying for, up or down. That size is the <b>priced move</b>. It says nothing about direction.</p>
<GuessGap />
<section class="blk">
  <p class="lab">How it is played</p>
  <p>Each report shows the priced move. You guess the size of the next day's move, close to close. Direction is not part of the guess.</p>
  <p>A guess within 2 points counts as a hit.</p>
</section>
